From: lancethepants <lancethepants@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:50:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] bpi-r3-mini: run fan PWM at 25kHz

Tomato64 deviation from the OpenWrt dts (00003). The fan header's third
pin is a PWM control input (no tach). At the upstream 10000ns period
(100kHz) the fan barely varies below full speed and stalls easily; fan
PWM inputs are specified for ~25kHz. At 40000ns the speed tracks duty
smoothly. The signal is inverted (255 = stop, 0 = full): 204 (~80%) is
the slowest level that reliably starts the fan from rest, 217 (85%)
does not.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a-bananapi-bpi-r3-mini.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a-bananapi-bpi-r3-mini.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a-bananapi-bpi-r3-mini.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a-bananapi-bpi-r3-mini.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a-bananapi-bpi-r3-mini.dts
@@ -75,8 +75,8 @@
 	fan: pwm-fan {
 		compatible = "pwm-fan";
 		#cooling-cells = <2>;
-		cooling-levels = <255 128 80 0>;
-		pwms = <&pwm 0 10000 0>;
+		cooling-levels = <255 204 128 0>;
+		pwms = <&pwm 0 40000 0>;
 		status = "okay";
 	};

--
